abstract: >-
  Let a(n) be the number of terms in the greedy representation of n by the
  Fibonacci and Lucas numbers (OEIS A214973). We prove Kimberling's
  conjecture that the ratio of the number of Zeckendorf summands of
  1, ..., n to a(1) + ... + a(n) tends to a limit in (1.2, 1.4); the limit
  is (5 - sqrt 5)/2, and |a(1) + ... + a(n) - (1/5) n log_phi n| <= 10n.
  We also prove the conjectures of Greathouse and Kurkov on A214973. Every
  statement is formalized in Lean 4.
